  "Full API spec": "All classes are in the default package (no package declarations). Allowed dependency direction: MediaItem -> Playlist -> PlayerState/VolumeControl/DeterministicClock -> PlayerSnapshot/PlaybackController -> Main -> MainTest. No circular dependencies. pom.xml: Maven build file compiling with source/target 11. Declares org.junit.jupiter:junit-jupiter (test scope only) and configures Maven Surefire Plugin 3.x to enable JUnit 5. No runtime dependencies. src/main/java/MediaItem.java: public final class MediaItem { public MediaItem(String id, String title, long durationMillis). Throws IllegalArgumentException if id or title is null/blank (trim length == 0) or if durationMillis <= 0. public String getId(); public String getTitle(); public long getDurationMillis(); Immutable semantics: fields are final and exposed via getters only. src/main/java/Playlist.java: public final class Playlist { public Playlist(); public void add(MediaItem item) — throws IllegalArgumentException if item is null; appends otherwise. public int size(); public MediaItem getAt(int index) — throws IndexOutOfBoundsException for invalid index (standard List semantics). public MediaItem removeAt(int index) — removes and returns item; throws IndexOutOfBoundsException for invalid index. public boolean hasNext(int index) — returns true iff nonempty and index < size()-1; safe for any index value within standard expectations. public boolean hasPrevious(int index) — returns true iff nonempty and index > 0. public int nextIndex(int index) — for empty list returns -1; for nonempty returns Math.min(Math.max(index,0)+1, size()-1) to clamp within [0, size-1]. public int previousIndex(int index) — for empty list returns -1; for nonempty returns Math.max(Math.min(index, size()-1)-1, 0). Backed by ArrayList<MediaItem> internally. src/main/java/PlayerState.java: public final class PlayerState { public static enum PlaybackStatus { STOPPED, PLAYING, PAUSED } private int currentIndex; private long positionMillis; private PlaybackStatus status; public PlayerState() — zero-arg constructor initializes currentIndex=0, positionMillis=0, status=PlaybackStatus.STOPPED; initializing currentIndex to -1 is forbidden. public int getCurrentIndex(); public void setCurrentIndex(int index) — no negative enforcement beyond caller usage. public long getPositionMillis(); public void setPositionMillis(long position) — throws IllegalArgumentException if position < 0; otherwise assigns. public PlaybackStatus getStatus(); public void setStatus(PlaybackStatus status) — throws NullPointerException if status is null. public void resetPosition() — sets positionMillis=0. } src/main/java/VolumeControl.java: public final class VolumeControl { private int volume; private int lastNonMuted; private boolean muted; public VolumeControl() — initializes volume=100, lastNonMuted=100, muted=false. public int getVolume(); public void setVolume(int volume) — validates 0 <= volume <= 100; throws IllegalArgumentException otherwise; always assigns this.volume = volume and this.lastNonMuted = volume, even if muted. public int getLastNonMuted(); public boolean isMuted(); public void mute() — sets muted=true without changing volume or lastNonMuted. public void unmute() — sets muted=false and restores volume = lastNonMuted. public int getEffectiveVolume() — returns muted ? 0 : volume. Note: setting volume while muted changes the value restored on unmute (e.g., set to 30 while muted -> unmute restores 30). } src/main/java/DeterministicClock.java: public final class DeterministicClock { private long currentTimeMillis; public DeterministicClock() — sets currentTimeMillis=0. public long getCurrentTimeMillis(); public void advance(long deltaMillis) — throws IllegalArgumentException if deltaMillis < 0; otherwise adds deltaMillis to currentTimeMillis. No wall clock use, sleeps, timers, randomness, or side effects. } src/main/java/PlayerSnapshot.java: public final class PlayerSnapshot { private final int index; private final String title; private final long positionMillis; private final long durationMillis; private final PlayerState.PlaybackStatus status; private final int volume; private final boolean muted; public PlayerSnapshot(int index, String title, long positionMillis, long durationMillis, PlayerState.PlaybackStatus status, int volume, boolean muted) — fully initializes fields; immutable with getters only. public int getIndex(); public String getTitle(); public long getPositionMillis(); public long getDurationMillis(); public PlayerState.PlaybackStatus getStatus(); public int getVolume(); public boolean isMuted(); public static PlayerSnapshot from(Playlist pl, PlayerState st, VolumeControl vc) — If pl is empty or st.getCurrentIndex() is invalid, returns a snapshot with title=\"\" and durationMillis=0 while reflecting state's index/position/status and volume/mute from vc. For valid index, reads MediaItem at that index for title/duration. } src/main/java/PlaybackController.java: public final class PlaybackController { private final Playlist playlist; private final VolumeControl volumeControl; private final DeterministicClock clock; private final PlayerState state; private long lastTick; public PlaybackController(Playlist playlist, VolumeControl volumeControl, DeterministicClock clock) — requires nonnull arguments; throws NullPointerException if any null; creates new PlayerState (currentIndex=0) and sets lastTick = clock.getCurrentTimeMillis(). public void play() — if playlist.size()==0, throws IllegalStateException; otherwise, if current position equals current duration (at end), resets position to 0; sets status=PLAYING (does not change index from 0 initial). public void pause() — sets status=PAUSED. public void stop() — sets status=STOPPED and resets position to 0. public void seek(long positionMillis) — clamps requested position to [0, current duration] and sets state's position accordingly; for empty playlist clamps to 0. public void next() — computes next index via playlist.nextIndex(currentIndex); if playlist is empty (-1), no-op; if index changes, updates currentIndex and resets position to 0; if at last index, remains there without resetting. public void previous() — analogous using playlist.previousIndex; reset position only when index actually changes; remain at first index at bounds. public void onClockAdvanced() — reads now = clock.getCurrentTimeMillis(); computes delta = Math.max(0, now - lastTick); sets lastTick = now; if state.status==PLAYING, advances position by delta; clamps position to duration; when position reaches or exceeds duration, sets position exactly to duration and sets status=STOPPED. public PlayerSnapshot getSnapshot() — returns PlayerSnapshot.from(playlist, state, volumeControl). public PlayerState getState(); public Playlist getPlaylist(); public VolumeControl getVolumeControl(); } src/main/java/Main.java: public final class Main { public static void main(String[] args) — constructs a small in-memory playlist (2–3 items), a VolumeControl and DeterministicClock, constructs PlaybackController, calls play(), advances clock by a small delta (e.g., 1000) and calls onClockAdvanced(), prints a brief snapshot line, and exits without loops or input. } src/test/java/MainTest.java: exactly three @Test methods using JUnit Jupiter. Test 1: single MediaItem duration 5000, new controller, play, clock.advance(5000), onClockAdvanced -> snapshot index 0, position 5000, duration 5000, status STOPPED. Test 2: two items (3000, 4000), play at index0; seek(5000) clamps to 3000; next -> index1 position0; next remains index1; previous -> index0; previous remains index0. Test 3: volume controls: setVolume(70), mute -> effective 0; setVolume(30) while muted -> getVolume 30 and effective 0; unmute -> getVolume 30 and effective 30. Deterministic-only, headless, offline; tests import only canonical public classes. Default-package rule applies to all source files.",
  "Shared Knowledge": "All production classes and Main.java are in the default package under src/main/java to avoid package/import mismatches. The build uses Maven with Java 11; org.junit.jupiter:junit-jupiter is test-scoped and Maven Surefire 3.x runs JUnit 5 tests. Core logic is separated from environment-dependent code: MediaItem, Playlist, PlayerState, VolumeControl, DeterministicClock, PlayerSnapshot, and PlaybackController form the pure core; Main.java is a thin, non-interactive runtime demo. The single test file src/test/java/MainTest.java imports only the canonical public classes (MediaItem, Playlist, PlayerState, VolumeControl, DeterministicClock, PlayerSnapshot, PlaybackController) and JUnit Jupiter APIs. Tests are deterministic and headless: they drive playback exclusively via DeterministicClock.advance(...) and PlaybackController.onClockAdvanced().",
  "Execution Protocol": "Test command: mvn -q test. Runtime entry: src/main/java/Main.java (default package). Single protocol-level test target: src/test/java/MainTest.java with exactly three @Test methods as specified. No manual interaction, no GUI, no filesystem/network/timers/randomness. Additional files are not introduced; all planned files adhere to the exact 10-file list.",
